commit 89adba63b21c10bd0289dd6d40e32eb82899a634
Author: Falconiere Barbosa <falconieer@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Jun 18 02:00:24 2026 -0300

    feat(plan-ledger): preflight gate, running state, and optional realtime dashboard
    
    Harden the execution phase and add an optional read-only kanban over the plan-ledger, keeping the ledger the single source of truth.
    
    Engine (bash+jq): preflight refuses execution until the plan is Approved and its declared spec (if any) is Approved, resolving status via a new pl_doc_field inline-bold header parser (new plan-ledger-preflight.sh keeps plan-ledger.sh under the size ceiling); the ledger gains a 'running' status + started_at/activity (version stays 1, additive — the push-gate denies version!=1); orphaned 'running' steps self-heal to pending past a stuck threshold; new path/root subcommands; the push-gate lists a running step as a blocker.
    
    Dashboard (Bun + vanilla JS + SSE, plugins/toolu/dashboard/): read-only realtime kanban that watches the ledger's parent dir (the writer renames via mv), re-arms + stat-poll fallback, and pushes initial state on SSE connect; git runs against the repo root so diff_sha matches the engine; never throws (absent ledger -> empty, git failure -> no false-stale, corrupt JSON -> error payload). Launch: bun run plugins/toolu/dashboard/index.ts [--open].
    
    Tests are real-data only (genuine git repos stamped by the real engine; no mocks) and cover the failure paths. Docs synced: execution/plan/plan-review SKILLs, README, contract bats. CI (test:ts glob + tsconfig include) extended to the dashboard.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d4c2294..86090a4 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -180,8 +180,19 @@ Beyond the plugins, the core (`toolu`) also ships:
 - **docs-sync backstop** — on `git push`, an **advisory** (never a block) when the branch diff changes code but no documentation surface (README, `docs/` guides, `SKILL.md` triggers) — a nudge to keep user-facing docs in sync with behavior. Silenced by a diff-`sha`-keyed attestation; surfaces are tunable via `docsSync.*` ([config](docs/config.md#docs-sync-surfaces-docssync)). Pairs with the "Docs in sync" convention the workflow skills enforce.
 - **Slash commands** — `/commit` and `/review-and-commit`.
 - **`deep-explore` agent** — structural codebase exploration via ast-grep.
+- **Execution dashboard** — an optional, read-only realtime kanban over the plan-ledger (see below).
 - **Caveman mode** — ultra-compressed, token-frugal output (via the `caveman` dependency).
 
+### Execution dashboard
+
+An optional, read-only **realtime kanban** over the plan-ledger — the ledger stays the single source of truth; the dashboard only watches it. It is **off by default** and nothing auto-starts it. Launch it from the repo root:
+
+```bash
+bun run plugins/toolu/dashboard/index.ts [--open]
+```
+
+It binds an ephemeral localhost port, prints the URL, and (with `--open`) opens your browser. Cards live in four columns driven by ledger status — **To Do** (pending) · **Running** (pulsing) · **Blocked** (red) · **Done** (green; amber + ↻ when a step's diff has gone stale) — and animate between columns as `plan-ledger.sh run` writes each step. It is **purely read-only**: no route mutates the ledger, so it can be closed or crash with zero effect on execution.
+
 ## Workflow skills
 
 A native, opinionated process chain. Each phase has a **write step and a review step**, so a design exists before planning and an audit happens before code is called done:
